Thanks for joining us.

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.000
This is OmniView Episode 100,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.740
balanced news perspectives.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.480
Today is July 2nd, 2026.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.740
Here's the news, the perspectives,

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.560
and the questions worth asking.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.400
That's Episode 100, a big milestone.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.040
Thank you for being here.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.940
Europe's top court upholds a record $4.7 billion fine

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.840
against Google, tightening oversight of dominant tech platforms

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.340
that shaped daily digital access for millions.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.440
The European Court of Justice rejected Alphabet's challenge

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.460
to a 2018 European Commission penalty of roughly $4.7 billion.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.760
The original ruling found Google had abused its Android dominance

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.340
by requiring device makers to pre-install its search and browser apps.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.820
The decision ends years of litigation

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.980
and requires payment of the fine.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.420
Both European regulators and technology firms

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.880
accept that Android holds a large share

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.580
of mobile devices in Europe.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.320
The disagreement centers on whether pre-installation deals

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.680
harmed competition or simply reflected consumer preference

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.080
for integrated services.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.820
European regulators view the outcome as validation of their authority

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.860
to curb practices that lock users into one company's ecosystem.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.300
Technology companies and some US officials

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.800
argue such fines risk fragmenting global markets

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.100
and slowing innovation by punishing successful scale.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.780
How do different legal systems define abuse of dominance?

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.660
Shifting now to Britain where the Prime Minister

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.320
will address a different kind of historical reckoning.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.260
Keir Starmer will apologize in Parliament

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.780
for policies between 1949 and 1976

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.320
that led to an estimated 185,000 babies being removed

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.820
from unmarried mothers in England and Wales.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.060
Campaigners and a commons committee have pressed

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.380
for both the statement and ongoing practical support.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.840
The government has not yet detailed

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.680
what follow-up measures will accompany the apology.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.020
Survivors and parliamentary committees emphasize

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.600
that an apology alone is insufficient

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.220
without concrete services such as counseling

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.420
and record access.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.900
Government statements frame the step

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.420
as recognition of past state coercion

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.560
while noting limits on what retrospective policy

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.140
can achieve decades later.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.540
What records remain available to affected families?

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.960
Next, a development in a long-running

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.560
energy infrastructure case.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.020
Prosecutors in Germany say a Ukrainian suspect

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.060
acted on orders from Ukrainian state authorities

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.400
when explosives were placed on the Nord Stream gas pipelines

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.540
in 2022.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.420
The suspect faces formal charges.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.400
Russia has long accused Ukraine of involvement.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.880
Kiev has denied state direction.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.120
German investigators present evidence they say

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.180
links the operation to official Ukrainian direction.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.920
Ukrainian officials maintain the attack

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.340
served no state interest and point to other possible actors

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.860
with access to the sites.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.260
What physical evidence has been made public so far?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.300
Meanwhile in North Africa, voters went to the polls yesterday.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.060
Voters in Algeria went to the polls on July 2nd

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.300
to elect a new parliament.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.740
Seven years after the Herak protest movement,

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.200
several opposition groups are participating this time,

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.180
though many citizens are still expected to abstain.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.900
Turn out in the previous election was 23%.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.880
Government officials present the vote

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.580
as a routine democratic exercise that demonstrates stability.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.660
Opposition voices and protest organizers

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.960
describe the process as offering limited real choice

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.600
and point to persistent economic grievances.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.860
Which changes, if any, have been made to electoral rules since 2019?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.320
Turning to travel infrastructure, Berlin Airport

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.080
is warning of major disruption later this year.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.640
The head of Berlin's airport stated that the EU's

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.580
new entry exit system will produce queues

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:02.360
that are not bearable during peak holiday periods.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.140
The system requires biometric data from non-EU travelers.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.200
Implementation is scheduled for later this year.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:13.940
Airport operators highlight practical capacity limits

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:17.880
at major hubs and call for phased rollout or extra staffing.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.800
EU officials stress the system's role

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.720
in improving security and tracking overstays.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.280
Which countries will be most affected by the new requirements?

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.360
In Indonesia, a Sharia court handed down

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.000
corporal punishment this week.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.520
A Sharia court in Ache province sentenced

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.820
an unmarried man and woman to 21 lashes each

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.700
after they were convicted of kissing during a live stream.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.720
The punishment was carried out in front of at least 100 witnesses.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:50.080
The province applies its own version of Islamic criminal law.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.760
Provincial authorities describe the sentence

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.240
as enforcement of local moral standards

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.980
that enjoy community support.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.600
Human rights organizations argue the public nature

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.400
of the punishment violates international standards

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.720
on corporal penalties.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.780
How does Ache's legal system interact

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.320
with Indonesia's national criminal code?

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:12.960
Finally, reports from Southern Africa

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:16.080
describe large-scale returns driven by protests.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.900
Protests demanding the removal of undocumented migrants

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.900
have led an estimated 15,000 people to return to Malawi.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.800
Demonstrators blame foreign nationals

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.280
for unemployment and crime.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.200
South African authorities and rights groups

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.040
dispute those causal claims.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.440
Protest organizers maintain that rapid migration

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.900
strains public services and job markets.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.900
Government and civil society groups counter

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.840
that migrants contribute economically

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.220
and that violence targets people based on nationality

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.700
rather than legal status.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.320
What legal pathways exist for migrants already in South Africa?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.740
Brazilian rail operator VLI-SA has opened a dedicated corridor

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.720
to move soy meal from interior growing regions to export ports.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.880
The new line is intended to reduce current transport constraints

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.300
that limit volumes from farms to ships.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.360
Brazil remains the top global supplier

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.980
of the animal feed ingredient.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.300
Agricultural shippers note the added capacity

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.760
could cut logistics expenses for producers.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.960
Environmental organizations raise concerns

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.140
that higher throughput may add pressure

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.420
on land conversion and forest cover.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.980
Observers on both sides agree

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.440
existing rail lines already constrain

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.500
how much product can leave the interior each season.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.580
Nvidia has rolled out a program that lets selected startups

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.800
exchange access to its processors

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.600
for a portion of future revenue

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.420
instead of paying cash upfront.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.480
The offer focuses on firms developing

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.420
artificial intelligence applications

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.940
that need large-scale training capacity.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.140
Contract details will differ

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.440
according to each customer's stage and project scope.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.480
Nvidia presents the arrangement as a method

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.880
to reduce early cash outlays while sharing upside.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.080
Some founders and investors have voiced worries

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.900
that the model might create lasting

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.680
supplier dependence or affect equity stakes.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.600
All parties recognize that advanced model

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.260
training demands significant computing resources.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.320
Meta has introduced a subscription requirement

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:24.400
for certain on-device artificial intelligence functions

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.780
in its smart glasses.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.860
The devices themselves continue to be sold

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.240
as a one-time purchase.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:32.720
The company states the recurring fee

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.720
will support ongoing development and cloud services.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.940
Consumer advocates contend the change lowers

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.900
the effective value of the original hardware outlay.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.440
Both Meta and Critics acknowledge

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.620
the glasses combine local processing

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.040
with cloud resources.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:51.120
The disagreement centers on whether subscriptions

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.020
represent an equitable method

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:54.740
to finance further upgrades.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.900
The Summer of Ludd Festival in New York City

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.920
is running workshops aimed at lowering

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.780
dependence on smartphones and social platforms.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.240
Organizers have designed sessions for younger adults

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:09.060
who report fatigue with continuous connectivity.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.200
Activities include practical exercises

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.080
for adjusting digital routines.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.320
Participants describe the gathering

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.400
as an opportunity to regain focus

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.220
and ease pressure from algorithm-driven content.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.600
Technology firms and digital economy voices

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.520
maintain that total disconnection is impractical

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.600
and that moderation tools already exist.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:34.080
Both groups recognize elevated screen time figures

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.400
among young adults.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:39.320
Arsonists set fire to a car owned by former boxer

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.780
Ricky Hatton outside his son's residence

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.060
in Greater Manchester.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.600
Police are classifying the incident

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.940
as a deliberate attack.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.000
No one was injured in the event.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.580
Local authorities have asked the public

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.720
for information on possible witnesses.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.380
Hatton's representatives have not released

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:58.680
any statement regarding suspected motives.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.240
Neighbors and investigators agree

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.280
the blaze was started intentionally.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.540
Now, to really understand the Google ruling

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.140
that opened today's episode,

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:10.880
there is something most coverage leaves out.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.400
Most reports assume the European Court of Justice

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.560
simply re-examines whether a company broke the rules.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.800
In practice, the court reviews whether the commission

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:24.200
followed its own procedures applied the correct legal tests

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.160
and set a proportionate penalty.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.400
It rarely retries the underlying facts.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.240
This structure means companies can succeed

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.920
on narrow procedural grounds,

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.800
even when the core finding of dominance stands.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.600
Knowing this distinction helps listeners

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.760
separate headlines about Google winning

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.780
from the narrower legal victories that sometimes occur.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:48.920
Next time you see a report on a fine being upheld or reduced,

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.660
ask which part of the commission's reasoning was actually challenged

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:55.600
and what precedent the ruling sets for future cases

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.500
involving similar market power.

